Running the  Combat.  Because the violet fungi 
move so slowly, it's easy for the characters to stay 
out of their reach and kill the fungus monsters 
with ranged attacks. The interesting part of this en­
counter is identifying the danger. One violet fungus 
moves and attacks to start the encounter, but the 
other two remain motionless until characters move 
close to them. 
You don't need to keep track of exactly where ev­
eryone is standing in  the room. Instead, rely on your 
sense of what's fun and exciting. When a character 
Three myconid sprouts named Bispo, Valup, and 
