SPELL  SCROLL 
Scroll,  Varies 
A spell scroll bears the words of a single spell, writ­
ten in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class's 
spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell 
without providing any material components. Other­
wise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell by 
reading the scroll requires the spell's normal cast­
ing time. Once the spell is cast, the words on the 
scroll fade, and it crumbles to dust. If the casting is 
interrupted, the scroll is not lost. 
If the spell is on your class's spell list but of a 
higher level than you can normally cast, you must 
make an ability check using your spellcasting ability 
to determine whether you cast it successfully. The 
DC equals  10 + the spell's level. On a success, you 
cast the spell; on a failure, the spell disappears from 
the scroll with no other effect. 
The level of the spell on the scroll determines the 
spell's saving throw DC and attack bonus, as well as 
the scroll's rarity, as shown in the Spell Scroll table. 
